# Introduction

In this workshop, you will act as a data analyst preparing **five focused data extracts for another analyst or stakeholder**. You will work with a real-world Lending Club dataset and use pandas to select columns, filter rows, combine logical conditions, rename fields, and export your results.

Your goal is not merely to obtain five CSV files. By the end, you should be able to explain **why each subset contains the right records and variables**, verify that its logic works, and make your workflow reproducible.

## Learning outcomes

By the end of the exercise, you should be able to:

1. Import a CSV dataset from an external GitHub source into Google Colab.
2. Inspect a DataFrame and use its data dictionary to interpret variables.
3. Select, remove, and rename columns using pandas.
4. Filter records using numerical comparisons and multiple logical conditions.
5. Distinguish **OR** conditions (any criterion) from **AND** conditions (all criteria).
6. Identify columns by name patterns and export separate, well-labelled datasets.
7. Validate each extract before submitting your notebook.

::: {.callout-tip title="Before you begin"}
Work sequentially. Keep the DataFrame name `loans_data` and the requested subset names exactly as written. If your code produces an error, read the message, consult the hints, and try again. Record questions to discuss during the live workshop.
:::

